      "concern": "F1 is \"def-feferman-tail-flip-definability-model identifies the ranked finite-predicate union M* with HS_F^G for that exact symmetric system\". That identification is a substantive two-sided equivalence (the reverse direction is Feferman's tail homogeneity plus V = L), but it is asserted inside a definition item whose provenance is not-applicable, with only a one-sentence sketch; the ZF theorem then consumes it as given. A judge should treat the equivalence itself, not only the transfer through the published symmetric-model theorem, as the load-bearing claim.",
